State-of-Health Estimation Methods
==================================

This repository contains standalone Python scripts for estimating battery State of Health (SOH)
and training machine-learning models using BMS data. The files are organized to make the
workflow and assets easy to find.

Repository layout
-----------------
assets/plots/
  Pre-generated result plots and figures.

scripts/soh_methods/
  SOH estimation approaches and pipelines:
  - soh_code_1.py
  - soh_code_2.py
  - soh_code_3.py
  - soh_pipeline.py
  - pybamm_calibration_vs.py

scripts/ml/
  ML training and evaluation scripts:
  - train_and_run_ml_rf_xgb.py
  - train_plus_ml.py
  - train_rf_xg_dnn.py

data/
  Place input datasets here.
  - CAN_Data_Dump_For_PINV502949_30-Aug_15_03_48.csv
  - CAN_Data_Dump_For_PINV502949_30-Aug_15_08_23.csv
  - battery SOH reference.csv
  - bms/ (folder with BMS CSV files for ML scripts)

outputs/
  Generated outputs (training datasets, model plots, and calibration artifacts).

Usage notes
-----------
- Run scripts from any working directory; they resolve paths relative to the repo root.
- Update the input file names in each script if your datasets use different names.
